Z||000000||8Ball||10-22-2001||09:31 PM||||Well I have been looking at my seriously faded almost gold Fiero, and wondering what it would look like without the grooved trim all the way around it. I know removeing it from the rear bumper is going to be a pain.<BR>So I have a few questions.<P>1. If I remove all the trim and fill in the grooves am I going to make my panels flap by not haveing those few screws there anymore?<P>2. What is the best way to remove the trim from the rear bumper?<P>3. What should I use to fill in the grooves where the trim used to be.<P>4. And finally about how hard is this task going to be.<P>P.S. Anyone have photos of what an aero bodied SE will look like without the trim?<P>Thanks everyone,<BR>Randy W.||||reg||5
